From c576e740ebb28d7f4bbf3a0d28f8c3d436b5148f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:08:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-152 GOAL 2 batch 1: ciru's Vulkan SPIRV-Headers
 fallback, tq3's f32 hybrid-SSM state gates, rocmfpx's -ffast-math guard

1. VULKAN - fall back to searching for SPIR-V headers instead of a hard REQUIRED. Ours was still `find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG REQUIRED)` at ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt line 14. Applied verbatim: QUIET first, then find_path over Vulkan_INCLUDE_DIRS and $ENV{VULKAN_SDK}/Include, and a clear FATAL_ERROR naming the fix instead of a bare package-not-found. Link the imported target when it exists, include the found directory when it does not. Our box already resolves the config package, so this changes nothing here today; it is taken because it is our platform and our backend and it removes a hard configure failure for any box whose Vulkan SDK ships the headers without the CMake config, which is the ordinary Windows SDK layout. CONTRACT: touches no type id, so FLAG C ("HQ call owed before ciru is ever used as a port source") does not gate it - that is a type-id gate and this diff is CMake only, checked against the diff rather than assumed.

2. QUANTIZE - keep hybrid-SSM state gates (ssm_alpha / ssm_beta / ssm_ba) in f32 by default. Applied into src/llama-quant.cpp; no `ssm_alpha` existed anywhere in ours. WHAT WE TOOK IS THE ARCHITECTURAL ARGUMENT, not the fork's benchmark: these tensors participate MULTIPLICATIVELY in the carried recurrent state of a hybrid SSM (DeltaNet / qwen3next), so quantization error compounds along the sequence instead of staying local to one matmul. The rule that follows - multiplicative state-update participants stay f32, readouts and projections may be quantized - is checkable from the architecture. User overrides still win (--tensor-type, --pure).

3. GGML-HIP - record why -ffast-math must not come back. COMMENT ONLY, because the code half is a DUPLICATE and it is SHOWN duplicated rather than assumed: our ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt has no -ffast-math at all, since upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp#26696 is already in our new base b10481. The reasoning is kept at the exact line where the flag would be re-added: -ffast-math implies -fassociative-math, which reassociates FP reductions and can flip greedy argmax on RDNA3.5 so MTP speculative decode diverges from the non-speculative baseline; -ffinite-math-only additionally lets the compiler assume inf/NaN cannot occur, so EXPM1 returns NaN where the CPU returns inf. rocmfpx carried this flag from its initial snapshot until 2026-08-17 and upstream removed it twice, so it is demonstrably re-introducible.

DECLINE DISCIPLINE for this batch, since the union law makes a DECLINE the thing that needs a reason: the only declines taken are BROKEN, DUPLICATE and NOISE. "Arrives with a backend we do not build" is NOT one of them - this fork ships CUDA and HIP source (the patch series carries a whole 4-other-backends layer), so such a commit is ordinary tree content whose only difference is that our smoke does not exercise it. prisml@4dd165625 (do not propagate the kv-mean-center bias to draft contexts) is DEFERRED, not declined: kv_mean_center_path does not exist anywhere in our tools/server/server-context.cpp, so the fix patches a prisml capability we have never ingested. The bias feature itself is the remainder item and that fix rides in with it.

EVERY number quoted below is the SOURCE FORK'S, measured on THEIR hardware, and none of it was reproduced on this box. No arm of any of those comparisons was run here.

Taken-from: ciru@8ffb2cd5a9b9e7eecc49335e0c79291a0df81d65
Origin: applied verbatim to ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt; ours was the hard REQUIRED.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED
Taken-from: tq3@b1dd18410620bbf16909444d95ee2f9c10015b085
Origin: applied verbatim to src/llama-quant.cpp; took the architectural rule, not their benchmark.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - the source reports reasoning depth 17k-64k to 33k-120k chars and
  structural codegen bugs eliminated on Qwen3.8-27B at tq3_4s, plus about 12 MiB per family of
  size cost. Theirs, not ours.
Taken-from: rocmfpx@8e6277f855df2a27ce072525ed19f3adc4138c47
Origin: comment only - the code half was already true here via upstream #26696 in base b10481.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - the source measured 60 to 14 test-backend-ops failures on
  gfx1151 / ROCm 7.14 at about 2 percent decode cost. We do not build HIP in the configuration
  any number in this repository was measured on.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt    | 10 ++++++++++
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/llama-quant.cpp                 | 14 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt
index 60384fa8e..105a04760 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -178,3 +178,13 @@ if (GGML_HIP_RCCL)
 endif()
 
 target_link_libraries(ggml-hip PRIVATE ggml-base hip::host roc::rocblas roc::hipblas)
+
+# NOTE: do not add -ffast-math / -funsafe-math-optimizations here. Upstream tried both and removed
+# them (ggml-org/llama.cpp#25495, #26696): they imply -fassociative-math, which reassociates FP
+# reductions and can flip greedy argmax on RDNA3.5, making MTP speculative decode diverge from the
+# non-speculative baseline. -ffinite-math-only additionally lets the compiler assume inf/NaN cannot
+# occur, so EXPM1 returns NaN where the CPU returns inf.
+# Guard only: this line is already absent here (upstream #26696 is in our base b10481). It is kept
+# as a comment because rocmfpx carried the flag from its initial snapshot until 2026-08-17 and had
+# to remove it again - the regression is re-introducible, so the reason is recorded where it would
+# be re-introduced.
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt
index b5652be51..c895ec2d3 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -11,7 +11,22 @@ find_package(Vulkan COMPONENTS glslc REQUIRED)
 if (DEFINED ENV{VULKAN_SDK})
     list(APPEND CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH "$ENV{VULKAN_SDK}")
 endif()
-find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG REQUIRED)
+find_package(SPIRV-Headers CONFIG QUIET)
+if (NOT TARGET SPIRV-Headers::SPIRV-Headers)
+    find_path(GGML_VULKAN_SPIRV_HEADERS_INCLUDE_DIR
+        NAMES
+            spirv/unified1/spirv.hpp
+            spirv-headers/spirv.hpp
+            spirv.hpp
+        HINTS
+            ${Vulkan_INCLUDE_DIRS}
+            "$ENV{VULKAN_SDK}/Include"
+    )
+    if (NOT GGML_VULKAN_SPIRV_HEADERS_INCLUDE_DIR)
+        message(FATAL_ERROR
+            "SPIR-V headers were not found. Install SPIRV-Headers or a complete Vulkan SDK.")
+    endif()
+endif()
 
 if (CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "MSVC")
     # Parallel build object files
@@ -111,6 +126,11 @@ if (Vulkan_FOUND)
 
     target_link_libraries(ggml-vulkan PRIVATE Vulkan::Vulkan)
     target_include_directories(ggml-vulkan PRIVATE ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR})
+    if (TARGET SPIRV-Headers::SPIRV-Headers)
+        target_link_libraries(ggml-vulkan PRIVATE SPIRV-Headers::SPIRV-Headers)
+    else()
+        target_include_directories(ggml-vulkan PRIVATE ${GGML_VULKAN_SPIRV_HEADERS_INCLUDE_DIR})
+    endif()
 
     # Workaround to the "can't dereference invalidated vector iterator" bug in clang-cl debug build
     # Possibly relevant: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/74748276/visual-studio-no-displays-the-correct-length-of-stdvector
diff --git a/src/llama-quant.cpp b/src/llama-quant.cpp
index ff02b9b3b..ee036894c 100644
--- a/src/llama-quant.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-quant.cpp
@@ -456,6 +456,20 @@ static ggml_type llama_tensor_get_type_impl(quantize_state_impl & qs, ggml_type
         return std::make_pair(i_layer, n_layer);
     };
 
+    // Hybrid SSM (e.g. DeltaNet / qwen3next): keep the recurrent state-update gates in f32 by default.
+    // These tensors participate MULTIPLICATIVELY in the carried recurrent state, so quantization error
+    // compounds along the sequence instead of staying local to one matmul. That is the whole argument
+    // and it is architectural, not empirical - the numbers below are the source fork's, not ours.
+    // Rule: tensors that participate multiplicatively in recurrent state updates stay f32; readouts
+    // and projections may be quantized. User overrides still win: --tensor-type <pattern>=<type> takes
+    // precedence and --pure quantizes everything as before.
+    // NOTE: can't use LLM_TN here because the layer number is not known.
+    if (name.find("ssm_alpha") != std::string::npos ||
+        name.find("ssm_beta")  != std::string::npos ||
+        name.find("ssm_ba")    != std::string::npos) {
+        return GGML_TYPE_F32;
+    }
+
     // for arches that share the same tensor between the token embeddings and the output, we quantize the token embeddings
     // with the quantization of the output tensor
     if (category == tensor_category::OUTPUT || (qs.has_tied_embeddings && category == tensor_category::TOKEN_EMBD)) {
